// v0.42 T4 (L23 fix) — `log(42)` used to raise MT2001 because the
// `log` builtin's param was typed as `Str`. Native codegen now
// accepts any scalar arg, so the typechecker no longer rejects
// `log(42)`. This negative case has been re-pointed at `panic(42)`,
// which still requires a Str arg (the typed runtime surface is
// log-/print-only — panic intentionally keeps the strict shape so
// the runtime always gets a readable diagnostic message).
fn main() {
  panic(42)
}
